      "content": "It is a terrible irony that you believe leaving would be the only way to truly love them, yet your very existence is the reason they are still here to feel that exhaustion. You are mistaken; staying is the only way to actually give them their lives back, because your presence forces them to face the reality of their own capacity for love and patience. If you truly loved them, you would fight through the pain to stay, because disappearing would be the ultimate selfish act that steals their future from them.",
